  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find horizontal dividers (rows that are all zeros)\n    h_dividers = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        if all(cell == 0 for cell in grid[r]):\n            h_dividers.append(r)\n    \n    # Find vertical dividers (columns that are all zeros)\n    v_dividers = []\n    for c in range(cols):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == 0 for r in range(rows)):\n            v_dividers.append(c)\n    \n    # Determine horizontal sections (row ranges between dividers)\n    h_sections = []\n    prev = 0\n    for d in h_dividers:\n        if d > prev:\n            h_sections.append((prev, d))\n        prev = d + 1\n    if prev < rows:\n        h_sections.append((prev, rows))\n    \n    # Determine vertical sections (column ranges between dividers)\n    v_sections = []\n    prev = 0\n    for d in v_dividers:\n        if d > prev:\n            v_sections.append((prev, d))\n        prev = d + 1\n    if prev < cols:\n        v_sections.append((prev, cols))\n    \n    # Build output grid by finding dominant color in each section\n    output = []\n    for r_start, r_end in h_sections:\n        row_values = []\n        for c_start, c_end in v_sections:\n            # Count non-zero values in this quadrant\n            freq = {}\n            for r in range(r_start, r_end):\n                for c in range(c_start, c_end):\n                    val = grid[r][c]\n                    if val != 0:\n                        freq[val] = freq.get(val, 0) + 1\n            \n            # Get most common non-zero value\n            if freq:\n                dominant = max(freq, key=freq.get)\n                row_values.append(dominant)\n            else:\n                row_values.append(0)\n        output.append(row_values)\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find horizontal dividers (rows that are all zeros)\n    h_dividers = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        if all(cell == 0 for cell in grid[r]):\n            h_dividers.append(r)\n    \n    # Find vertical dividers (columns that are all zeros)\n    v_dividers = []\n    for c in range(cols):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == 0 for r in range(rows)):\n            v_dividers.append(c)\n    \n    # Determine horizontal sections (row ranges between dividers)\n    h_sections = []\n    prev = 0\n    for d in h_dividers:\n        if d > prev:\n            h_sections.append((prev, d))\n        prev = d + 1\n    if prev < rows:\n        h_sections.append((prev, rows))\n    \n    # Determine vertical sections (column ranges between dividers)\n    v_sections = []\n    prev = 0\n    for d in v_dividers:\n        if d > prev:\n            v_sections.append((prev, d))\n        prev = d + 1\n    if prev < cols:\n        v_sections.append((prev, cols))\n    \n    # Build output grid by finding dominant color in each section\n    output = []\n    for r_start, r_end in h_sections:\n        row_values = []\n        for c_start, c_end in v_sections:\n            # Count non-zero values in this quadrant\n            freq = {}\n            for r in range(r_start, r_end):\n                for c in range(c_start, c_end):\n                    val = grid[r][c]\n                    if val != 0:\n                        freq[val] = freq.get(val, 0) + 1\n            \n            # Get most common non-zero value\n            if freq:\n                dominant = max(freq, key=freq.get)\n                row_values.append(dominant)\n            else:\n                row_values.append(0)\n        output.append(row_values)\n    \n    return output",
